id=a52sxq_bixby_wakeup_guard
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: "Hi Bixby" voice wake-up with the A52s keyword models
author=kusti420
description=The S26 Ultra Bixby Wakeup app sends its keyword model (an asset, kwdModel/<mode>/<locale>/<keyword>.bin) straight to the ADSP; the A52s ADSP firmware faults on that newer model revision in its LPI voice module (err_qdi.c audio_process LPro00dyn) and the SoC resets, and the app reloads it after every boot - a boot loop (9.3.30 refused these models altogether). The A52s stock app's models (same names, same sizes, the Hi Bixby ones differ only in their last field) are now extracted from the target firmware into /system/etc/k4wakeup, and the sound trigger middleware swaps the app's model for the A52s one of the same name (found by matching the bytes in the installed app, Galaxy Store update or system copy). Models without an A52s counterpart (new modes, Japanese) are still refused, so the ADSP never sees a model its firmware did not ship with. persist.sys.k4.samsung_wakeup=1 passes models through unchanged (debugging only), =2 refuses all of them (kill switch).
